{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789256315,"nonce":"RWGbYNk/fqhDYyk3GO8Z+v+Xa5o=","title":"OSR entry at a range loop compared the interpreter's exhausted iterator","message":"The range-loop pass rewrites for (i in a...b) into a counted loop whose header compares the counter with the bound. The interpreter's iterator register for the same loop holds false once Range.iterate runs out, and the back-edge probe that fires at exactly that point entered the compiled header with it: 'Bool does not implement \u003c(_)'. Intermittent (1-4 in 30 runs of bench/ash/nbody.wren, whenever the baseline install landed on the last iteration), and present with the top tier off. The pass now records the counter in speculated_num_params so the entry declines a non-Num and the interpreter exits the loop itself.","files":null}]}